      "Okafor's letter",
      "Ada —\n\nI'm writing this because I won't say it on the radio. Nothing I care about goes on the radio any more. It keeps what it hears.\n\nI love you. I love Chidi. I always meant him to have the stamps.\n\nIf this reaches you and I don't, tell him his father counted heads every night for two years, and the number was always forty-one — and then one night it was forty-two, and nobody could tell me who the extra one was.\n\n— T."
     ]
